    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "What is Python: History features and the different  between Python 2 and python 3.\n",
        "\n",
        "---> Python is a high-lvel, interpreted and general purpose programming language know for its emphasis on code readability and clear syntax. Created by Guido va ROssum and first released in 1991, its desigh philosophy emphasizes code readability with the use of significant indentation.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Brif History of python\n",
        "\n",
        "*   The Beginning (Late 1980s) :  Guido van rossum began working on Python in December  1989 at Centrum Wiskunde and Informatica (CWI) in the Netherlands and a succesor to the ABC programming language.\n",
        "*   Interpreterd Language : Code is executed line by line , which is simplifier dubugging\n",
        "*  Dynamically Types: You don't need to explicitly declare the data type of a variable. Python determines it at runtime.\n",
        "* Extensive Standard libraty: it comes with a massive collections of modules and package\n",
        "* Corss-Platform : Python run seamlessly on windown, macos , linux and unix all.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6_0hiLtE1svs"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "Variables : Rules of identifiers , assiging values and dynamic typing\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "TgkIznht4_uz"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 1. Rules for Python Identifiers\n",
        "An identifier is a name userd to identify a variable, function  and class , moules or other object. TO avoid syntax error , you  must  follow these rules when naming variables in python.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "* Allow Characters: Must start with a letter (A-Z, a-z) or an underscore (_), followed by letters, digits(0-9) or underscores.\n",
        "* No Number at the Start: A variable name cannot begin with a number ( eg. 1st_variable is invalid; variable_1 is valid)\n",
        "* Case Sensitive : Python is case-sensitive , meaning age, Age and AGE are three completely different variables.\n",
        "* No Special Characters: Symbols like @, $, and  % are not allowed.\n",
        "* Reserved Keywords: You cannot use Python's build-in keywords ( such as if , else, while, calss, def, import ) as variable names."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ewBe-Ge75Umo"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "## Assigning Value to Variables\n",
        "## Python uses the equal sign (=) as the assignment operator to bind a value to a variable name.\n",
        "x=10\n",
        "name = \"PRabhaw\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(x , name)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "OY9ErKrZ9plI",
        "outputId": "af1856a2-881e-436d-cd19-fc7476bbc724"
      },
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "10 PRabhaw\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "## Multiple Assignment\n",
        "x, y, z = 1, 2, 3\n",
        "print(x, y, z)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "50R-_mce-Avk",
        "outputId": "f3f6a922-d515-4fe0-8668-9b0a9d45913e"
      },
      "execution_count": 6,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "1 2 3\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "## Chain Assigment\n",
        "x = y = z = 10\n",
        "print(x, y, z)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "9n8LzHyv-MDP",
        "outputId": "c2deee2f-5bd5-4d7b-8f03-e3fbd92d9033"
      },
      "execution_count": 8,
