          "text": [
            "10 10 10\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Dynamic Typing\n",
        "Python is a dynamically typed language. This means you don not need to explicitly declare the data type of a variable when you create it.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "*  Hot it work : Under the hood, a Python variable is simply a reference ( or label ) pointing to an object stored in memory. The data type belongs tho the object. not the variable name.\n",
        "*   Rassignment: Because of dynamic typping , you can easily change the type of data a variable holds during program execution.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "GU3TCm_05Uce"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "x = 10\n",
        "print(type(x))\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "nmrMCISd-Vxp",
        "outputId": "95e0645d-e4c1-438d-9251-5d6049a356c2"
      },
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "<class 'int'>\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "x= \"hello\"\n",
        "print(type(x))"
      ],
