    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Basic Data type\n",
        "Every value in python has as specific data ytype. Knowing your data type help you understand what kid of operation you can perform on a piece of data.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 1 . Integers (int )\n",
        "Integers represend whole number - positive, neagtive, or zero - without any decimal or fractional part. Python integers have nulimited precision ( their size is only limited by your system's available memory)\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ot--J8NS_RSn"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "age = 25\n",
        "temperature = -5\n",
        "population = 10000000"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "OsbH6mtb_Lb5"
      },
      "execution_count": 11,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "## Operator : You can perform standard arthemetic operations like addition (+),\n",
        "## subtraction (-)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HZR5mYLpAh9B"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 2. Float (float)\n",
        "Float (floating point numbers) represent real numbers that contain a decimal point or area writtten in scientific notation.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "td7oCivfAxYs"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "pi = 3.14159\n",
        "height = 5.9\n",
        "scientific_notion = 1.5e2\n",
        "\n",
        "print(pi, height, scientific_notion)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
