    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Typecasting ( also know as type conversion ) is the process of converting a variable or value from one data type to another. Pyton support two types of typecasting : Implicit and Explicit."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "jyB8Yzw4Jou2"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "## 1. Implicit Typecasting (Automatic)\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "In implicit type, Python automatically convert one data type to another without any\n",
        "user intervention. THis usaually happends when mixing data type in an operation to prevent data\n",
        "loss.\n",
        "\n",
        "\"\"\""
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 71
        },
        "id": "6e-BUwEIDqaA",
        "outputId": "9e01eafa-605d-4277-ab61-5ef43c43cc2a"
      },
      "execution_count": 25,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "' \\nIn implicit type, Python automatically convert one data type to another without any\\nuser intervention. THis usaually happends when mixing data type in an operation to prevent data\\n\\n\\n'"
            ],
            "application/vnd.google.colaboratory.intrinsic+json": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 25
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "## How it works: Python automatically upgrade a lower data type\n",
        "##like an integer to a higher data type (like a float) during mapt operations."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "kiuyB0XVKIcl"
      },
      "execution_count": 26,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
