          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 2. Explicit typecasting (Manual)\n",
        "In pxplicit typecasting, the programmer manually converts a data type using Python's build-in conversion functions. THis is also known as type coercion."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "NPHUlX2MK9hw"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# the primay build itn fucntions:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dZmcaRdyLRNV"
      },
      "execution_count": 28,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "x = 10.5\n",
        "print(int(x))\n",
        "print(float(x))\n",
        "print(str(x))\n",
        "print(bool(x))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "dAdGy87fLO6R",
        "outputId": "464aa9d2-28b5-414b-d359-5153e01c65ae"
      },
      "execution_count": 29,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "10\n",
            "10.5\n",
            "10.5\n",
            "True\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 1. Arithmetic & Assignment Operators\n",
        "Arithmetic Operators: Used for standard math (+, -, *, /, //, %, **). For example, 10 % 3 gives the remainder 1.\n",
        "\n",
        "Assignment Operators: Used to assign values to variables, often combined with an arithmetic operation (shorthand notation):\n",
        "\n",
        "= (Assign): x = 5\n",
        "\n",
        "+= (Add and assign): x += 3 (equivalent to x = x + 3)\n",
        "\n",
        "-= (Subtract and assign): x -= 2\n",
        "\n",
        "*= (Multiply and assign): x *= 4"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hpc1QDuGQ7Ab"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 2. Comparison & Logical Operators\n",
        "Comparison Operators: Compare two values and return a Boolean (==, !=, >, <, >=, <=). Example: 5 < 10 evaluates to True.\n",
        "\n",
        "Logical Operators: Combine conditional statements (and, or, not).\n",
        "\n",
        "and: Returns True if both conditions are true.\n",
        "\n",
        "or: Returns True if at least one condition is true.\n",
        "\n",
        "not: Reverses the Boolean outcome."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "CL4ya6orQ_dT"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 3. Identity Operators (is, is not)\n",
        "Identity operators compare the memory locations of two objects, not just their values. (This is different from ==, which checks if the values are equal).\n",
        "\n",
        "is: Returns True if both variables point to the exact same object in memory.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "is not: Returns True if they do not point to the same object."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "kmdEeu7zRHJV"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "x = [1, 2, 3]\n",
        "y = [1, 2, 3]\n",
        "print(x == y)  # True (values are equal)\n",
        "print(x is y)  # False (different objects in memory)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "SYCDhvbFRKCK",
        "outputId": "d9b43f3b-0215-4a99-cf19-c99b8ba75519"
      },
      "execution_count": 31,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "True\n",
            "False\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "dNFXupovRLkC"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 4. Membership Operators (in, not in)\n",
        "Membership operators are used to test if a value is present within a sequence (like strings, lists, tuples, or dictionaries).\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "PQAlrY4ARSPG"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "## in: Returns True if the specified value is found in the sequence.\n",
        "fruits = [\"apple\", \"banana\", \"cherry\"]\n",
        "print(\"banana\" in fruits)  # Output: True"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "eJF07XMlRUuN"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "## not in: Returns True if the specified value is not found in the sequence."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Dy_59VG-RbRe"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "print(\"grape\" not in fruits)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "EvU6i7N7ReXp"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 5. Bitwise Operators\n",
        "Bitwise operators act on operands as if they were strings of binary digits (0s and 1s). They operate bit by bit:"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AEEBosOjRjnU"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "print(5&3)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "agnq8Jj8RqdV",
        "outputId": "ef57210d-fbf7-4003-adb0-f3d6421e9533"
      },
      "execution_count": 32,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "1\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "print(5 | 3)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "icXrEuX4TYwT",
        "outputId": "6f0bd119-8407-4ea1-8717-5e7976dfb8a6"
      },
      "execution_count": 33,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "7\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "print(5 ^ 3)"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
